-- title:
--   Numerical work budget for one finishing-table entry
-- statement:
--   For natural numbers $n,E,B$, representing the ground size, an encoding-size budget for counts, and a size budget for multipliers, respectively, the per-entry finishing budget is the explicit polynomial
--   $$\operatorname{finishEntryBudget}(n,E,B)=3n^2+E+10+4E^2+2(B+4E)^2.$$
--   This bundle defines the numerical budget used in the finishing-scan resource analysis. It does not itself prove an execution bound. Resource quantities in this development are counters for the declared charged operations, rather than verified physical-machine or bit-stack costs.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/FinishPhaseWork.lean#L38-L41

